     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That's about twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. Single doses are also usually capped at about 850\u20131000 mg. Doses this high greatly raise the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nCan you tell me which of these you meant?\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **850 mg PO three times daily** with meals, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily** with meals, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Another dose.** If 1700 mg three times daily is truly what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
